    "narrative": "The heart of our lineup today rests on the high-efficiency matchup for **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Avila in a favorable park environment. **Taylor Ward** serves as our strongest play, leveraging a +16% park factor and a +19% advantage against a pitcher with an xERA approaching 5.00, securing him the highest daily efficiency score on the roster. While **Dylan Beavers** deals with an \"Elite Hold\" tag that slightly suppresses his SB potential against a tough pickoff pitcher, his overall hitting environment allows him to maintain a high floor. We are also capitalizing on **Bryce Harper** (68.39) in the middle of the order, as his xwOBA of .399 against Flaherty suggests he is well-positioned to drive in runs even against a reasonably difficult arm. \n\nStrategic lineup optimization forced some difficult decisions, most notably the benching of **Daulton Varsho** (53.53). While **Daulton Varsho** offers the elite sprint speed we covet for our stolen base category, his matchup against a left-handed starter and a negative platoon split tipped the scales in favor of **Jonathan Aranda** (61.98), whose right-handed bat against a righty starter provides a more robust projection across the board. We are also keeping a close eye on **JJ Bleday** (56.85); while his platoon edge against Imanaga keeps him in the starting nine, the 35% rain risk serves as a potential volatility trap. Elsewhere, **Lawrence Butler** is poised to capitalize on a +13% platoon edge and the leadoff spot, while **Gavin Sheets** provides unexpected stability with a +19% SP skill boost against a vulnerable Bieber. We are proceeding with the current configuration, monitoring weather reports for **JJ Bleday** closely as we navigate the scarcity of our SB targets.",
